From 4e03ca9c15a8448fd2fc2d28a37ecb0aa3aa0027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jorink <maxjorink@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:41:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spotlight: draw the menu like macOS Spotlight

A search field in a glass pill with a magnifier and a placeholder, the
results below it with the apps' icons (desktop entries, hicolor; PNG or
SVG through nanosvg) and the highlighted one in a blue rounded row.
680 px wide, centred a fifth of the way down. The compositor draws the
glass behind the surface; this draws a light tint and a hairline rim.

On by default; BEMENU_SPOTLIGHT=0 restores bemenu's own look. Needs
nanosvg.h and nanosvgrast.h in lib/renderers/.
